/*
Can you count and say what characters the string '11121' has?
It has three '1' characters, followed by one '2', 
and finally one '1'. Or to put it another way, it has 3 1s, 1 2s and 1 1, 
which we could write as the string '311211'. For this problem, we define 
this transformation as "counting and saying". Counting and saying '11121' is '311211'.
For this problem, you have to generate a sequence given an Integer N. 
We define base case for N = 1 as '1'. For N > 1, count and say the sequence generated by N - 1.

*/

public string countAndSay(integer N) {
    if(N == 1){
        return '1';
    }

    String anterior = countAndSay(N - 1);
    String result = '';
    Integer count = 0;

    for(Integer i = 0; i < anterior.length(); i++){
        count++;
        if(i == anterior.length() - 1 || !anterior.charAt(i).equals(anterior.charAt(i + 1))){
            result += String.valueOf(count) + anterior.substring(i, i+1);
            count = 0;
        }

    }

    return result;
}